          "post": {
            "id": "2066207953355432118",
            "url": "https://x.com/x-user-1/status/2066207953355432118",
            "content": {
              "text": "There are two types of engineers in 2026\n\nThe first opens his laptop in the morning, writes a prompt, waits, reads the diff, fixes it, repeats\n\nThe second opens his phone, checks what shipped while he was asleep\n\nDifferent answer to one question: who is the loop?\n\nThe first engineer is the loop, he starts the agent, reviews the output, decides what's next, the moment he steps away it stops\n\nThe second engineer built the system that is the loop instead of him, PR review, flaky tests, CI triage, all running without him, he just reads the report\n\nWhat stops most people isn't complexity\n\nIt's that they never noticed they are the bottleneck\n\nFull guide to building the system that runs without you below",
              "media_urls": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2066207862070595584/img/qhWvfwj5fx_gcnrK.jpg",
