        {
          "post": {
            "id": "2094410530932797945",
            "url": "https://x.com/x-user-13/status/2094410530932797945",
            "content": {
              "text": "I spent 3 days debugging a flaky test in 2021. The element was there, then it wasn’t. I added sleep(5000). I prayed. It still failed.\n\nThen we migrated to Playwright. Auto-wait actually worked. Network interception meant I didn't have to mock a database just to test a frontend toggle. My test suite went from taking 45 minutes to 6 minutes.\n\nStop fighting your framework. If you are still adding hard sleeps to your tests in 2026, it’s time to move on.\n\nWhat was your \"I can't believe we used to do it the old way\" moment in automation? 👇",
              "media_urls": null,
              "thumbnail_url": null,
              "duration_seconds": null
            },
